1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,831
Every time an app loads something, it asks a question, and it gets an answer.

2
00:00:05,381 --> 00:00:06,557
Open a weather app.

3
00:00:06,557 --> 00:00:09,528
It asks a server: what is the weather in Boston?

4
00:00:09,528 --> 00:00:11,881
The server answers: sixty-one degrees,

5
00:00:11,881 --> 00:00:12,314
cloudy.

6
00:00:12,864 --> 00:00:15,120
That question is called a request.

7
00:00:15,120 --> 00:00:17,243
The answer is called a response.

8
00:00:17,243 --> 00:00:18,570
Today you read both,

9
00:00:18,570 --> 00:00:19,433
line by line,

10
00:00:19,433 --> 00:00:20,693
with real commands.

11
00:00:21,243 --> 00:00:22,829
Because when an app breaks,

12
00:00:22,829 --> 00:00:27,174
the first thing a dev ops engineer checks is the request and the response.

13
00:00:29,224 --> 00:00:33,811
A request has four parts: a method, a path, headers, and sometimes a body.

14
00:00:34,361 --> 00:00:35,922
The method is the verb.

15
00:00:35,922 --> 00:00:37,823
It says what you want to do.

16
00:00:37,823 --> 00:00:38,842
Get means read.

17
00:00:38,842 --> 00:00:40,064
Post means create.

18
00:00:40,064 --> 00:00:41,422
Delete means remove.

19
00:00:41,972 --> 00:00:47,455
The path says which thing. Slash API slash products slash one means: product number one.

20
00:00:48,005 --> 00:00:50,221
Headers are labels about the message,

21
00:00:50,221 --> 00:00:52,258
like what kind of data it carries.

22
00:00:52,258 --> 00:00:53,935
The body is the data itself.

23
00:00:54,485 --> 00:00:58,453
The response has three parts: a status code, headers, and a body.

24
00:00:59,003 --> 00:01:02,583
The status code is a three digit number that says how it went.

25
00:01:02,583 --> 00:01:04,315
It is the first thing to read.

26
00:01:06,365 --> 00:01:11,208
Let us send a real request. Go into the shop. Type: CD, cloud cart.

27
00:01:11,758 --> 00:01:17,774
This version of cloud cart has a full API. Start it. Type: dot slash start dot S H.

28
00:01:18,324 --> 00:01:20,305
Ask for product number one.

29
00:01:20,305 --> 00:01:23,828
The dash I flag also shows the response headers.

30
00:01:23,828 --> 00:01:24,635
Type: curl,

31
00:01:24,635 --> 00:01:25,149
dash I,

32
00:01:25,149 --> 00:01:29,993
local host colon five thousand slash API slash products slash one.

33
00:01:30,543 --> 00:01:31,887
Read it from the top.

34
00:01:31,887 --> 00:01:33,935
The first line says two hundred,

35
00:01:33,935 --> 00:01:34,191
O K.

36
00:01:34,191 --> 00:01:36,303
That is the status code: success.

37
00:01:36,853 --> 00:01:37,893
Then the headers.

38
00:01:37,893 --> 00:01:40,217
Content type says the body is jay son.

39
00:01:40,217 --> 00:01:42,357
Content length says how many bytes.

40
00:01:42,907 --> 00:01:44,484
And after the blank line,

41
00:01:44,484 --> 00:01:46,313
the body: the product itself.

42
00:01:46,313 --> 00:01:47,637
That was one request,

43
00:01:47,637 --> 00:01:48,710
and one response.

44
00:01:49,260 --> 00:01:51,305
Now ask for the whole list.

45
00:01:51,305 --> 00:01:52,138
Type: curl,

46
00:01:52,138 --> 00:01:52,668
dash s,

47
00:01:52,668 --> 00:01:56,909
local host colon five thousand slash API slash products,

48
00:01:56,909 --> 00:01:57,288
pipe,

49
00:01:57,288 --> 00:01:57,591
J Q,

50
00:01:57,591 --> 00:01:58,121
dash C,

51
00:01:58,121 --> 00:01:58,576
quote,

52
00:01:58,576 --> 00:02:00,091
dot bracket bracket,

53
00:02:00,091 --> 00:02:00,545
quote.

54
00:02:01,095 --> 00:02:01,879
Same address,

55
00:02:01,879 --> 00:02:03,508
without the one at the end.

56
00:02:03,508 --> 00:02:05,077
Now you get every product.

57
00:02:05,077 --> 00:02:07,068
The path decides what comes back.

58
00:02:09,118 --> 00:02:10,931
That body is written in jay son.

59
00:02:11,481 --> 00:02:14,169
It stands for java script object notation,

60
00:02:14,169 --> 00:02:16,153
but every language can read it,

61
00:02:16,153 --> 00:02:18,649
so it is the common language of A P Is.

62
00:02:19,199 --> 00:02:21,242
Curly braces hold one object.

63
00:02:21,242 --> 00:02:23,497
Each field has a name in quotes,

64
00:02:23,497 --> 00:02:24,061
a colon,

65
00:02:24,061 --> 00:02:25,117
then the value.

66
00:02:25,117 --> 00:02:26,527
Text goes in quotes.

67
00:02:26,527 --> 00:02:27,583
Numbers do not.

68
00:02:28,133 --> 00:02:29,846
Square brackets hold a list.

69
00:02:29,846 --> 00:02:31,437
Commas separate the items.

70
00:02:31,437 --> 00:02:32,476
Forget one comma,

71
00:02:32,476 --> 00:02:34,128
and the whole thing breaks.

72
00:02:34,678 --> 00:02:38,689
J Q reads jay son and prints it tidy. You will use it every day.

73
00:02:40,639 --> 00:02:44,564
Same shop, new session. Go in. Type: CD, cloud cart.

74
00:02:45,114 --> 00:02:48,165
Start it. Type: dot slash start dot S H.

75
00:02:48,715 --> 00:02:52,072
What if you ask for something that does not exist?

76
00:02:52,072 --> 00:02:53,415
Product ninety-nine.

77
00:02:53,415 --> 00:02:54,154
Type: curl,

78
00:02:54,154 --> 00:02:54,758
dash s i,

79
00:02:54,758 --> 00:02:55,564
the address,

80
00:02:55,564 --> 00:02:55,900
pipe,

81
00:02:55,900 --> 00:02:56,236
head,

82
00:02:56,236 --> 00:02:56,840
dash one,

83
00:02:56,840 --> 00:02:58,720
to show only the first line.

84
00:02:59,270 --> 00:03:04,070
Four oh four. Not found. The server understood you, but there is no such product.

85
00:03:04,620 --> 00:03:06,972
Good servers explain in the body too.

86
00:03:06,972 --> 00:03:08,371
Type the same request,

87
00:03:08,371 --> 00:03:09,579
without the dash i,

88
00:03:09,579 --> 00:03:10,914
to see only the body.

89
00:03:11,464 --> 00:03:12,757
Now a bad request.

90
00:03:12,757 --> 00:03:13,979
Create a product,

91
00:03:13,979 --> 00:03:15,703
but leave out the price.

92
00:03:15,703 --> 00:03:16,494
Type: curl,

93
00:03:16,494 --> 00:03:17,141
dash s i,

94
00:03:17,141 --> 00:03:18,218
dash capital X,

95
00:03:18,218 --> 00:03:18,578
post,

96
00:03:18,578 --> 00:03:19,081
dash d,

97
00:03:19,081 --> 00:03:21,165
the jay son in single quotes,

98
00:03:21,165 --> 00:03:22,386
then the address,

99
00:03:22,386 --> 00:03:22,746
pipe,

100
00:03:22,746 --> 00:03:23,105
head,

101
00:03:23,105 --> 00:03:23,752
dash one.

102
00:03:24,302 --> 00:03:27,779
Four hundred. Bad request. The fault is in what you sent.

103
00:03:28,329 --> 00:03:29,271
Now the pattern.

104
00:03:29,271 --> 00:03:30,920
Two hundreds mean it worked.

105
00:03:30,920 --> 00:03:33,569
Four hundreds mean the client made a mistake.

106
00:03:33,569 --> 00:03:35,689
Five hundreds mean the server broke.

107
00:03:36,239 --> 00:03:37,941
That one idea saves hours.

108
00:03:37,941 --> 00:03:40,101
Four hundred: check your request.

109
00:03:40,101 --> 00:03:42,980
Five hundred: check the server and its logs.

110
00:03:45,030 --> 00:03:47,292
Most A P Is follow a style called rest.

111
00:03:47,292 --> 00:03:49,147
Every thing has its own address,

112
00:03:49,147 --> 00:03:51,409
and the method says what to do with it.

113
00:03:51,959 --> 00:03:56,268
The thing is a noun. Here it is products, at slash API slash products.

114
00:03:56,818 --> 00:03:59,159
Get on that address reads the list.

115
00:03:59,159 --> 00:04:00,899
Get with an I D reads one.

116
00:04:00,899 --> 00:04:02,438
Post creates a new one.

117
00:04:02,438 --> 00:04:03,709
Delete removes one.

118
00:04:04,259 --> 00:04:08,995
Same address, different verbs. Learn these four, and you can read almost any API.

119
00:04:09,545 --> 00:04:13,513
There are also put and patch, for updating. Today we use these four.

120
00:04:15,563 --> 00:04:20,875
Now change data. Same shop, new session. Go in. Type: CD, cloud cart.

121
00:04:21,425 --> 00:04:24,476
Start it. Type: dot slash start dot S H.

122
00:04:25,026 --> 00:04:27,177
Create a product with post.

123
00:04:27,177 --> 00:04:29,010
Dash X sets the method.

124
00:04:29,010 --> 00:04:33,074
Dash H adds a header that says the body is jay son.

125
00:04:33,074 --> 00:04:35,146
Dash d is the body: a mug,

126
00:04:35,146 --> 00:04:36,023
price nine.

127
00:04:36,023 --> 00:04:37,378
Then the address.

128
00:04:37,928 --> 00:04:38,672
Two oh one.

129
00:04:38,672 --> 00:04:39,213
Created.

130
00:04:39,213 --> 00:04:42,799
The location header says where the new product lives.

131
00:04:42,799 --> 00:04:45,032
The body shows its new I D: four.

132
00:04:45,582 --> 00:04:47,267
Ask for the list again.

133
00:04:47,267 --> 00:04:48,074
Type: curl,

134
00:04:48,074 --> 00:04:48,587
dash s,

135
00:04:48,587 --> 00:04:49,466
the address,

136
00:04:49,466 --> 00:04:49,833
pipe,

137
00:04:49,833 --> 00:04:50,126
J Q,

138
00:04:50,126 --> 00:04:50,639
dash C,

139
00:04:50,639 --> 00:04:51,079
quote,

140
00:04:51,079 --> 00:04:52,545
dot bracket bracket,

141
00:04:52,545 --> 00:04:52,984
quote.

142
00:04:53,534 --> 00:04:54,803
The mug is there.

143
00:04:54,803 --> 00:04:56,220
The change is real,

144
00:04:56,220 --> 00:04:57,861
saved in the database.

145
00:04:57,861 --> 00:04:58,906
Now remove it.

146
00:04:58,906 --> 00:04:59,726
Type: curl,

147
00:04:59,726 --> 00:05:00,398
dash s i,

148
00:05:00,398 --> 00:05:01,517
dash capital X,

149
00:05:01,517 --> 00:05:02,039
delete,

150
00:05:02,039 --> 00:05:04,128
the address of product four,

151
00:05:04,128 --> 00:05:04,501
pipe,

152
00:05:04,501 --> 00:05:04,874
head,

153
00:05:04,874 --> 00:05:05,545
dash one.

154
00:05:06,095 --> 00:05:09,700
Two oh four. No content. Success, with nothing to say.

155
00:05:10,250 --> 00:05:15,050
Count what is left. Type: curl, dash s, the address, pipe, J Q, length.

156
00:05:15,600 --> 00:05:19,867
Three again. Stop the shop. Type: dot slash stop dot S H.

157
00:05:21,917 --> 00:05:25,501
Now see what a customer sees. This is the shop page, before.

158
00:05:26,051 --> 00:05:28,756
I created a mug and deleted the notebook,

159
00:05:28,756 --> 00:05:30,009
using only the API.

160
00:05:30,009 --> 00:05:32,252
Reload the page: the mug is there,

161
00:05:32,252 --> 00:05:33,902
and the notebook is gone.

162
00:05:34,452 --> 00:05:38,718
The page was never edited. Only the data behind the API changed.

163
00:05:39,268 --> 00:05:41,422
That is why the backend is separate.

164
00:05:41,422 --> 00:05:43,277
Any client can change the data,

165
00:05:43,277 --> 00:05:44,772
and every client sees it.

166
00:05:46,822 --> 00:05:49,595
Your task, in your own Ubuntu virtual machine.

167
00:05:50,145 --> 00:05:52,705
The lab is lab sixty-eight dot S H,

168
00:05:52,705 --> 00:05:56,436
in the academy slash lab folder of git hub dot com,

169
00:05:56,436 --> 00:05:57,898
slash it dash waves,

170
00:05:57,898 --> 00:05:59,581
slash dev ops dash A I.

171
00:05:59,581 --> 00:06:01,263
Install it like before,

172
00:06:01,263 --> 00:06:02,433
then run lab up.

173
00:06:02,983 --> 00:06:06,267
Cloud cart starts with its API on port five thousand.

174
00:06:06,267 --> 00:06:07,940
Five things need your work,

175
00:06:07,940 --> 00:06:08,807
all with curl.

176
00:06:09,357 --> 00:06:13,176
One: create a product named mug, price nine, once. Use post.

177
00:06:13,726 --> 00:06:16,158
Two: delete product number three, the notebook.

178
00:06:16,708 --> 00:06:18,410
Three: in answers dot text,

179
00:06:18,410 --> 00:06:20,993
write the status code your post returned,

180
00:06:20,993 --> 00:06:22,191
like this: created,

181
00:06:22,191 --> 00:06:22,569
colon,

182
00:06:22,569 --> 00:06:23,577
then the number.

183
00:06:24,127 --> 00:06:28,014
Four: do the same for asking for a product that does not exist,

184
00:06:28,014 --> 00:06:29,371
with the word missing.

185
00:06:29,371 --> 00:06:32,148
Five: and for a post with the price left out,

186
00:06:32,148 --> 00:06:33,258
with the word bad.

187
00:06:33,808 --> 00:06:36,347
Then run lab check. Five pass lines.

188
00:06:38,397 --> 00:06:40,381
Six points, and you need all six.

189
00:06:40,931 --> 00:06:42,808
The checker shows five pass lines.

190
00:06:43,358 --> 00:06:48,222
You can point at the method, the path, and the status code in a curl dash i output.

191
00:06:48,772 --> 00:06:51,546
You can explain four hundreds against five hundreds.

192
00:06:52,096 --> 00:06:54,528
You can create and delete a product with curl.

193
00:06:55,078 --> 00:06:59,302
You can read jay son: an object, a list, a text value, and a number.

194
00:06:59,852 --> 00:07:02,582
You ran lab down, and nothing is left listening.

195
00:07:03,132 --> 00:07:04,754
To pass, you need all six.

196
00:07:06,804 --> 00:07:09,641
Your turn, in your own Ubuntu virtual machine.

197
00:07:10,191 --> 00:07:12,410
One: install the lab, and run lab up.

198
00:07:12,960 --> 00:07:17,163
Two: ask for product one with curl dash i, and read the status line.

199
00:07:17,713 --> 00:07:19,633
Three: create the mug with post.

200
00:07:20,183 --> 00:07:21,825
Four: delete product three.

201
00:07:22,375 --> 00:07:25,469
Five: write answers dot text, then run lab check.

202
00:07:26,019 --> 00:07:27,491
